A question concerning all this - what happens if you change your
alignment? A monster's peaceful/hostile status won't change when you
change your alignment - a bug, IMHO. So for instance, as a lawful
character, I can have a peaceful white unicorm and a hostile black
unicorn on the level. If I then change my alignment to chaotic, the
white unicorn will still be peaceful and the black one of my alignment
will still remain hostile. So, now if I kill that peaceful white
unicorn as a chaotic, will I lose the luck? - or if I kill that
hostile black unicorn of my alignment that's thrashing on me, will I
also lose luck? In other words, do you lose luck for killing a
peaceful unicorn or is it one of your alignment, or both?

